Gitea 28.2.0 registers every OAuth2 source with goth once, with a callback URL
built from ROOT_URL (createProvider in services/auth/source/oauth2/providers.go),
and goth bakes it into oauth2.Config.RedirectURL. A sign-in started on another
public URL of the same instance, such as the onion vhost, is therefore sent back
to the ROOT_URL host. That host carries no cookie of the session that holds the
gothic state, so the callback fails with "could not find a matching session for
this request". Gitea's own OIDC sign-out already takes its redirect from
httplib.GuessCurrentAppURL (buildOIDCEndSessionURL in routers/web/auth/oauth.go).

Callout replaces the redirect_uri of the authorization URL with the callback URL
under httplib.GuessCurrentAppURL, and Callback hands the same value to goth as
the redirect_uri callback parameter, which the openidConnect session of goth
v1.82.0 sends in the token request instead of the registered one. On the
ROOT_URL host both equal the registered callback URL, and
PUBLIC_URL_DETECTION=never keeps ROOT_URL for every request. The other goth
providers ignore that parameter and still send the registered callback URL in
the token request, so only OpenID Connect sources gain sign-in on a second
public URL.

Generated with `diff -u` against the gitea-src-28.2.0 tarball and applied with
`git apply`, which allows no fuzz, so the build fails instead of landing a hunk
somewhere upstream moved it to.

